@startuml class-diagram
title Freelance Invoice Tracker - Class Diagram (Part 1 baseline)

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
hide empty members

' =========================
' Web layer (Express routes)
' =========================
package "UI Controllers" {
  class ClientController {
    - store : LocalStorageHandler
    + createClient(name : string, email : string) : Client
    + listClients() : Client[]
  }

  class ProjectController {
    - store : LocalStorageHandler
    + createProject(name : string, clientId : number) : Project
    + listProjects() : Project[]
  }

  class InvoiceController {
    - store : LocalStorageHandler
    + createInvoice(form : object) : Invoice
    + listInvoices() : Invoice[]
    + changeStatus(invoiceId : number, newStatus : string) : void
    + applyLateFee(invoiceId : number, amount : number) : number
    + applyDiscount(invoiceId : number, percent : number) : number
    + runOverdueCheck(today : Date) : void
  }
}

' =========================
' Storage
' =========================
package "Storage" {
  class LocalStorageHandler {
    - key : string
    + load() : object
    + save(data : object) : void
  }
}

' =========================
' Domain model
' =========================
package "Domain Model" {
  class Client {
    - id : number
    - name : string
    - email : string
  }

  class Project {
    - id : number
    - name : string
    - client : Client
  }

  class Invoice {
    - id : number
    - project : Project
    - issueDate : Date
    - dueDate : Date
    - status : string
    - billingType : string
    - hourlyRate : number
    - hoursLogged : number
    - fixedAmount : number
    - monthlyRate : number
    - months : number
    - hasLateFee : boolean
    - lateFeeAmount : number
    - hasDiscount : boolean
    - discountPercent : number
    + Invoice(id, project, issueDate, dueDate, billingType,\n hourlyRate, hoursLogged, fixedAmount, monthlyRate, months)
    + calculateTotal() : number
    + changeStatus(newStatus : string) : void
    + checkOverdue(today : Date) : void
    + applyLateFee(amount : number) : void
    + applyDiscount(percent : number) : void
    + toDisplayString() : string
  }
}

note right of Invoice::status
  "DRAFT" | "SENT" | "PAID" | "OVERDUE"
  changeStatus() checks every allowed
  move in one if/else chain
end note

note right of Invoice::billingType
  "HOURLY" | "FIXED" | "RETAINER"
  calculateTotal() switches on this
  and then adds the late fee and
  discount if their flags are set
end note

' =========================
' Relationships
' =========================
Client "1" o-- "0..*" Project : has >
Project "1" o-- "0..*" Invoice : has >

ClientController --> LocalStorageHandler
ProjectController --> LocalStorageHandler
InvoiceController --> LocalStorageHandler

ClientController ..> Client : <<create>>
ProjectController ..> Project : <<create>>
InvoiceController ..> Invoice : <<create>>

note as Planned
  <b>Known design problems and the patterns we plan to apply</b>
  ----
  Invoice is a God Object (SRP): status rules, billing math,
  fees/discounts and display text all live in one class.
  * status if/else chain (SRP, OCP) -> <b>State</b>
  * billingType switch in calculateTotal() (OCP) -> <b>Strategy</b>
  * fee/discount flags, no status check (OCP, risk 2) -> <b>Decorator</b>
  Controllers call new Client/Project/Invoice themselves
  (GRASP Creator, Low Coupling) -> <b>Factory Method</b>
  Each controller creates its own LocalStorageHandler (DIP)
  -> inject storage from main.js, as in the Todo App
  Invoice constructor has 10 parameters (telescoping
  constructor) -> <b>Builder</b> (optional)
end note

@enduml
